66
00:02:43,685 --> 00:02:45,115
(Stretching)

67
00:02:45,955 --> 00:02:47,025
My gosh.

68
00:02:47,355 --> 00:02:49,235
- She's groaning a lot this morning. - She's...

69
00:02:54,295 --> 00:02:55,725
Hello.

70
00:02:55,865 --> 00:02:59,134
I've been living alone for three years.

71
00:02:59,135 --> 00:03:02,004
I'm a member of Girls' Generation and an actress, Kwon Yu Ri.

72
00:03:02,005 --> 00:03:03,335
(Singer and Actress Yu Ri)

73
00:03:03,675 --> 00:03:07,405
I live on the east side of Jeju Island.

74
00:03:09,775 --> 00:03:10,975
You live on Jeju Island.

75
00:03:11,075 --> 00:03:12,275
It's one of my fantasies.

76
00:03:12,785 --> 00:03:14,145
(It's not frequented by tourists.)

77
00:03:14,415 --> 00:03:16,295
Why did you decide to live in the eastern part?

78
00:03:16,385 --> 00:03:19,055
I felt this bright energy from the eastern part.

79
00:03:20,525 --> 00:03:21,884
Gosh, how nice.

80
00:03:21,885 --> 00:03:24,245
- It's a single-family house. - It's a single-family house.

81
00:03:24,455 --> 00:03:27,025
In Jeju, we call it living on a yearly lease.

82
00:03:27,125 --> 00:03:28,464
- Right. - We don't put down a big deposit.

83
00:03:28,465 --> 00:03:29,665
We rent houses...

84
00:03:29,795 --> 00:03:32,765
on a yearly basis to live here.

85
00:03:33,365 --> 00:03:36,005
I also rented this house on a yearly basis.

86
00:03:37,035 --> 00:03:38,635
(Walking into her house...)

87
00:03:39,975 --> 00:03:41,105
It looks neat.

88
00:03:41,375 --> 00:03:43,215
How relaxing. It's nice and clean.

89
00:03:44,215 --> 00:03:47,445
Jeju Island was the first place I ever lived alone.

90
00:03:47,945 --> 00:03:49,785
I could decorate the house to my own taste...

91
00:03:50,115 --> 00:03:52,455
and do things just the way I wanted.

92
00:03:52,585 --> 00:03:54,755
- I was free to do that. - Right.

93
00:03:56,595 --> 00:03:57,924
Right. It's nice and simple.

94
00:03:57,925 --> 00:03:59,641
(Her own paintings are hanging all over the house.)

95
00:03:59,665 --> 00:04:01,965
(Exuding the Jeju vibe...)

96
00:04:03,235 --> 00:04:04,694
- This shows her personality. - Right.

97
00:04:04,695 --> 00:04:05,775
(are the cute decor items.)

98
00:04:06,665 --> 00:04:09,935
This house has almost everything I like.

99
00:04:10,735 --> 00:04:12,275
How did you end up moving there?

100
00:04:12,775 --> 00:04:15,875
- First of all, I love yoga. - Okay.

101
00:04:16,075 --> 00:04:18,375
- I also love nature. - Okay.

102
00:04:18,475 --> 00:04:20,244
In Seoul, I've always been...

103
00:04:20,245 --> 00:04:22,144
- so busy with work. - Right.

104
00:04:22,145 --> 00:04:24,655
I sought out a slower pace of life.

105
00:04:24,815 --> 00:04:26,425
- That's why. - I think I can guess it.

106
00:04:26,785 --> 00:04:27,984
- I can guess the yearly rent. - Okay.

107
00:04:27,985 --> 00:04:29,055
- How? - How much?

108
00:04:29,525 --> 00:04:32,865
I bet it's around 10,000 dollars. Or is it 9,000 dollars?

109
00:04:33,395 --> 00:04:34,824
- You're in the ballpark. - I am, right?

110
00:04:34,825 --> 00:04:36,194
- You're so close. - Have you looked into houses?

111
00:04:36,195 --> 00:04:38,294
- Yes. Jeju Island... - Right. It's Jeju Island.

112
00:04:38,295 --> 00:04:40,605
My mother used to have yearly leases too.

113
00:04:40,905 --> 00:04:44,475
- Yes. It's under 9,000 dollars. - He was spot on.

114
00:04:44,975 --> 00:04:46,805
- It's lower than that? - Yes, much lower.

115
00:04:46,945 --> 00:04:49,575
- It's much lower than that. - It's very cheap.

116
00:04:49,945 --> 00:04:52,465
- You found a good home then. - That's a really good deal then.

117
00:04:56,215 --> 00:04:59,085
(She goes to the bathroom as soon as she wakes up.)

118
00:05:00,225 --> 00:05:03,455
(She brushes her teeth right away.)

119
00:05:05,295 --> 00:05:07,825
(Tying her hair)

120
00:05:09,865 --> 00:05:13,305
(She thoroughly washes her face.)

121
00:05:16,905 --> 00:05:18,335
(Refreshed)

122
00:05:20,445 --> 00:05:21,545
Nice.

123
00:05:23,945 --> 00:05:25,915
(Walking over)

124
00:05:26,815 --> 00:05:28,745
(It's located right in front of the bathroom.)

125
00:05:29,955 --> 00:05:30,985
My dressing table.

126
00:05:32,285 --> 00:05:33,925
You don't have a lot of cosmetics.

127
00:05:34,055 --> 00:05:36,324
- I rarely need to wear makeup. - Right.

128
00:05:36,325 --> 00:05:38,695
Okay.

129
00:05:39,725 --> 00:05:41,964
(Pumping)

130
00:05:41,965 --> 00:05:43,094
All right.

131
00:05:43,095 --> 00:05:44,235
(Pumping)

132
00:05:44,795 --> 00:05:46,865
(Spreading it without hesitation)

133
00:05:47,205 --> 00:05:49,735
(Applying the leftover on her body)

134
00:05:49,875 --> 00:05:50,935
Sunscreen.

135
00:05:53,445 --> 00:05:55,174
You always wear sunscreen.

136
00:05:55,175 --> 00:05:57,114
I sometimes apply sunscreen instead of lotion.

137
00:05:57,115 --> 00:05:59,035
(I sometimes apply sunscreen instead of lotion.)

138
00:06:00,015 --> 00:06:02,855
(She roughly applies it on her face.)

139
00:06:04,355 --> 00:06:05,414
All done.

140
00:06:05,415 --> 00:06:06,524
(Wiping the residue on her body)

141
00:06:06,525 --> 00:06:07,624
All done.

142
00:06:07,625 --> 00:06:08,924
(She's done with her all-in-one skincare routine.)

143
00:06:08,925 --> 00:06:10,725
- That's it for your face? - Yes.

144
00:06:11,255 --> 00:06:12,554
She doesn't even put on essence.

145
00:06:12,555 --> 00:06:15,194
It takes about the same amount of time as my skincare routine.

146
00:06:15,195 --> 00:06:16,265
I bet.

147
00:06:16,935 --> 00:06:18,065
Okay.

148
00:06:19,065 --> 00:06:20,305
Gosh, it's so humid.

149
00:06:22,165 --> 00:06:24,175
(Opening)

150
00:06:25,605 --> 00:06:27,505
But the air must feel so fresh.

151
00:06:27,675 --> 00:06:29,244
She breathes in fresh air every morning.

152
00:06:29,245 --> 00:06:31,315
- She lives on Jeju Island. - Right.

153
00:06:38,015 --> 00:06:41,155
(Lifting something)

154
00:06:44,655 --> 00:06:45,794
- A dehumidifier? - Is it a dehumidifier?

155
00:06:45,795 --> 00:06:46,894
- It's that humid? - That's how much moisture...

156
00:06:46,895 --> 00:06:48,025
it collects in a day.

157
00:06:48,225 --> 00:06:49,694
The alarm wakes me up.

158
00:06:49,695 --> 00:06:52,094
- It means the dehumidifier is full. - Really?

159
00:06:52,095 --> 00:06:54,405
- I wake up at the alarm. - That's a lot of water.

160
00:06:54,635 --> 00:06:57,275
I have to keep the dehumidifier on all the time.

161
00:06:57,605 --> 00:07:00,105
I live right by the beach.

162
00:07:00,545 --> 00:07:02,045
So it's super humid.

163
00:07:02,305 --> 00:07:04,015
Jeju Island is definitely more humid.

164
00:07:04,715 --> 00:07:06,944
- That's why she's studying houses. - That's why.

165
00:07:06,945 --> 00:07:09,585
- The wallpaper is coming loose. - You can't do anything about it.

166
00:07:11,055 --> 00:07:13,585
Right. There's a leak. My mom's place has a leak too.

167
00:07:14,255 --> 00:07:16,925
- Well, it's an island, after all. - Right.

168
00:07:18,555 --> 00:07:19,864
- Right. - Moisture absorbers.

169
00:07:19,865 --> 00:07:21,171
- Moisture absorbers. - I can't live without them.

170
00:07:21,195 --> 00:07:22,824
Here's my routine. When I wake up,

171
00:07:22,825 --> 00:07:25,595
I empty out the dehumidifier which is filled to the brim.

172
00:07:25,995 --> 00:07:29,065
I empty it out three times a day in summer.

173
00:07:30,235 --> 00:07:33,005
(After emptying out the water from the dehumidifier, )

174
00:07:33,945 --> 00:07:37,315
(she turns it back on immediately.)

175
00:07:39,745 --> 00:07:42,315
(She lights a scented candle after turning on a dehumidifier.)

176
00:07:43,585 --> 00:07:44,714
(She's lighting more than one?)

177
00:07:44,715 --> 00:07:48,825
These scented candles help reduce humidity in my house.

178
00:07:48,925 --> 00:07:52,925
Lighting scented candles became part of my routine.

179
00:07:53,025 --> 00:07:55,324
- Yes. People should light them. - Right.

180
00:07:55,325 --> 00:07:57,995
(Humming)

181
00:07:58,395 --> 00:08:00,234
(Shaking her legs)

182
00:08:00,235 --> 00:08:01,334
She's excited.

183
00:08:01,335 --> 00:08:02,804
She easily gets excited.

184
00:08:02,805 --> 00:08:04,175
(Shaking her legs)

185
00:08:05,105 --> 00:08:09,305
(After lighting the scented candles, she keeps on humming.)

186
00:08:09,675 --> 00:08:13,115
(She grabs a vacuum cleaner and goes to the living room.)

187
00:08:13,315 --> 00:08:14,844
My gosh.

188
00:08:14,845 --> 00:08:18,255
(She plugs in the power cord.)

189
00:08:18,985 --> 00:08:20,484
(Tossing the cord over her shoulder)

190
00:08:20,485 --> 00:08:22,555
She threw the power cord over her shoulder.

191
00:08:23,655 --> 00:08:25,124
A lot of people have switched over...

192
00:08:25,125 --> 00:08:26,664
- to cordless vacuum cleaners. - Right.

193
00:08:26,665 --> 00:08:28,895
But I bought most of my household items...

194
00:08:29,295 --> 00:08:31,895
from a secondhand marketplace.

195
00:08:32,135 --> 00:08:34,104
- The table. - Really?

196
00:08:34,105 --> 00:08:36,505
And the sofa too. It was only 30 dollars.

197
00:08:36,935 --> 00:08:38,704
- I bought my fridge on the app. - Right.

198
00:08:38,705 --> 00:08:40,474
- You bought everything used. - Actually, I found the listing...

199
00:08:40,475 --> 00:08:41,545
- on the app too. - What?

200
00:08:41,675 --> 00:08:43,614
- The house too? - That's common on the island.

201
00:08:43,615 --> 00:08:45,244
- You found your house on the app? - Yes.

202
00:08:45,245 --> 00:08:49,115
- I guess so. It's robust. - This app has a robust community.

203
00:08:49,585 --> 00:08:52,085
- Yu Ri is so frugal. - Totally.

204
00:08:53,385 --> 00:08:58,995
(She cleans every nook and corner with a used vacuum cleaner.)

205
00:09:01,995 --> 00:09:03,935
I need to give more attention to these corners.

206
00:09:04,495 --> 00:09:06,064
(Suddenly turning off the vacuum cleaner)

207
00:09:06,065 --> 00:09:07,065
What's going on?

208
00:09:07,635 --> 00:09:09,104
What do I do with this spider?

209
00:09:09,105 --> 00:09:10,135
- My gosh. - Oh, no.

210
00:09:10,635 --> 00:09:12,805
Jeju Island is great, but there are a lot of bugs.

211
00:09:12,975 --> 00:09:14,174
You have to compromise on certain things...

212
00:09:14,175 --> 00:09:15,744
- when you live there. - Right.

213
00:09:15,745 --> 00:09:18,345
I have to live with bugs. But they scare me every time.

214
00:09:19,685 --> 00:09:23,555
(She grabs a paper cup from the cabinet.)

215
00:09:27,085 --> 00:09:28,825
Hey, spider.

216
00:09:30,425 --> 00:09:32,255
(Catching it on her first try)

217
00:09:34,025 --> 00:09:35,095
There it is.

218
00:09:35,925 --> 00:09:37,235
I should release it.

219
00:09:38,295 --> 00:09:39,564
She's going to spare it.

220
00:09:39,565 --> 00:09:41,104
- She caught it alive. - She should spare it.

221
00:09:41,105 --> 00:09:42,465
(Sliding)

222
00:09:44,535 --> 00:09:46,274
(Safely delivering it back to nature)

223
00:09:46,275 --> 00:09:47,404
Have a good life.

224
00:09:47,405 --> 00:09:49,175
Great job. She spared it.

225
00:09:53,285 --> 00:09:56,555
(Let me see.)

226
00:09:57,315 --> 00:09:59,885
(Grabbing a plastic bag)

227
00:10:00,085 --> 00:10:01,324
(Frowning)

228
00:10:01,325 --> 00:10:02,855
- What is it? - I bet there are bugs.

229
00:10:03,025 --> 00:10:04,694
- She must've seen something. - There must be bugs in there.

230
00:10:04,695 --> 00:10:05,995
(Scratching)

231
00:10:06,365 --> 00:10:07,365
Come on.

232
00:10:07,366 --> 00:10:09,024
- Gosh, why so many legs? - What's that?

233
00:10:09,025 --> 00:10:11,265
- It looks like a camel cricket. - It's a camel cricket.

234
00:10:11,935 --> 00:10:12,935
(Screaming)

235
00:10:14,305 --> 00:10:16,875
(I can do this.)

236
00:10:17,735 --> 00:10:20,845
(But she's struggling to catch it as it's the biggest one yet.)

237
00:10:22,275 --> 00:10:23,995
- The body is split in half. - My goodness!

238
00:10:24,875 --> 00:10:26,675
- I hate bugs. - It's not a cockroach, right?

239
00:10:26,985 --> 00:10:28,084
I don't think it is.

240
00:10:28,085 --> 00:10:30,184
(She barely manages to take care of it.)

241
00:10:30,185 --> 00:10:31,215
Come on.

242
00:10:34,525 --> 00:10:35,625
Goodbye.

243
00:10:36,755 --> 00:10:37,855
Goodbye.

244
00:10:38,395 --> 00:10:40,064
- "Goodbye." - "Goodbye."

245
00:10:40,065 --> 00:10:41,465
- She has a kind heart. - I got it.

246
00:10:42,925 --> 00:10:44,094
(This is it for me.)

247
00:10:44,095 --> 00:10:45,765
Seriously. This is killing me.

248
00:10:46,505 --> 00:10:49,565
(Exhausted)

249
00:10:50,435 --> 00:10:51,604
(Her cleaning session comes to an abrupt end.)

250
00:10:51,605 --> 00:10:52,634
Okay.

251
00:10:52,635 --> 00:10:54,475
(Her cleaning session comes to an abrupt end.)

252
00:10:54,675 --> 00:10:56,644
(Yu Ri comes into the kitchen after getting changed.)

253
00:10:56,645 --> 00:10:57,975
Good job.

254
00:10:58,645 --> 00:10:59,914
I started to talk to myself a lot...

255
00:10:59,915 --> 00:11:01,014
- when I began living alone. - Of course.

256
00:11:01,015 --> 00:11:02,384
- I didn't get why people did that. - Right.

257
00:11:02,385 --> 00:11:04,185
- It's... - But I became one of them.

258
00:11:04,355 --> 00:11:06,014
I need to eat something.

259
00:11:06,015 --> 00:11:07,855
(Talking to herself again)

260
00:11:08,125 --> 00:11:09,185
What will she eat?

261
00:11:10,155 --> 00:11:12,594
Let me take out the yam.

262
00:11:12,595 --> 00:11:13,665
She's taking what out?

263
00:11:15,625 --> 00:11:16,734
(The yam is frozen.)

264
00:11:16,735 --> 00:11:17,765
Yam?

265
00:11:17,935 --> 00:11:20,035
- You froze the yam? - Yes. I like yam.

266
00:11:20,135 --> 00:11:23,635
(She grabs milk and an apple too.)

267
00:11:25,575 --> 00:11:26,675
(Rustling)

268
00:11:28,405 --> 00:11:31,475
(Transferring the frozen yam pieces first)

269
00:11:32,815 --> 00:11:34,414
(Too big to go in)

270
00:11:34,415 --> 00:11:36,085
(Let me see.)

271
00:11:39,685 --> 00:11:42,525
- She's so down-to-earth. - Yu Ri is just like us.

272
00:11:42,785 --> 00:11:44,901
- That's the most effective way. - She's just like us.

273
00:11:44,925 --> 00:11:47,025
She's just like one of us. Right.

274
00:11:47,695 --> 00:11:48,794
Okay.

275
00:11:48,795 --> 00:11:50,634
(The yam is broken into small pieces.)

276
00:11:50,635 --> 00:11:52,165
(Feeling proud)

277
00:11:52,965 --> 00:11:55,034
(Adding apple pieces as well)

278
00:11:55,035 --> 00:11:56,834
I've been following this routine for 20 years now.

279
00:11:56,835 --> 00:11:57,904
- Really? - Yes.

280
00:11:57,905 --> 00:11:59,545
- Apples. - You've had yams for 20 years?

281
00:12:00,005 --> 00:12:02,404
(She adds milk...)

282
00:12:02,405 --> 00:12:03,844
(and honey too.)

283
00:12:03,845 --> 00:12:06,314
My mother used to make this for me since high school.

284
00:12:06,315 --> 00:12:08,084
- Oh, this? - Yes. A lot of moms used to...

285
00:12:08,085 --> 00:12:09,644
- make this shake. - I had to drink it for breakfast.

286
00:12:09,645 --> 00:12:11,454
Right. My mom used to make this too.

287
00:12:11,455 --> 00:12:13,015
(She's been blending it for 20 years.)

288
00:12:14,485 --> 00:12:16,894
This yam juice helped me boost my energy.

289
00:12:16,895 --> 00:12:18,771
- It's good for immune system too. - I should try that.

290
00:12:18,795 --> 00:12:19,895
The weather...

291
00:12:20,665 --> 00:12:22,465
Let me check the weather.

292
00:12:23,165 --> 00:12:24,535
The weather...

293
00:12:25,295 --> 00:12:28,265
(Looking up the weather on Jeju Island)

294
00:12:28,605 --> 00:12:30,535
Gosh, what a relief.

295
00:12:30,735 --> 00:12:32,435
It won't rain today.

296
00:12:33,745 --> 00:12:35,945
Okay. Nice.

297
00:12:36,475 --> 00:12:38,015
No rain forecast on AccuWeather.

298
00:12:38,945 --> 00:12:40,885
No rain forecast on the Weather Channel.

299
00:12:41,815 --> 00:12:43,785
No rain forecast on the news either.

300
00:12:43,985 --> 00:12:45,414
It won't rain. It'll just be cloudy.

301
00:12:45,415 --> 00:12:47,025
Does it rain often on the island?

302
00:12:47,185 --> 00:12:49,155
The weather affects me a lot.

303
00:12:49,785 --> 00:12:53,124
- I do a lot of outdoor activities. - I see.

304
00:12:53,125 --> 00:12:54,264
You're like a haenyeo. You're checking the weather.

305
00:12:54,265 --> 00:12:56,495
- Right. - Well, that's my dream.

306
00:12:57,295 --> 00:12:58,834
(Yu Ri checks the weather like a haenyeo.)

307
00:12:58,835 --> 00:12:59,835
Okay.

308
00:12:59,836 --> 00:13:01,764
(Meanwhile, her breakfast is ready.)

309
00:13:01,765 --> 00:13:04,374
Okay. I don't think I can make it by 7pm.

310
00:13:04,375 --> 00:13:06,744
(The yam juice she's been drinking for 20 years)

311
00:13:06,745 --> 00:13:07,775
(Humming in approval)

312
00:13:09,705 --> 00:13:12,574
Her diet reminds me of my grandmother.

313
00:13:12,575 --> 00:13:14,744
- Right. - Her diet is very healthy.

314
00:13:14,745 --> 00:13:17,155
My grandmother was 110 years old when she passed.

315
00:13:17,285 --> 00:13:19,245
Your routine is very similar to my grandmother's.

316
00:13:23,395 --> 00:13:26,665
Let me get ready to go out. All done. Okay.

317
00:13:27,465 --> 00:13:29,025
I should get changed now.

318
00:13:30,065 --> 00:13:31,834
(She quickly changes her outfit to go out.)

319
00:13:31,835 --> 00:13:33,405
She's going out.

320
00:13:34,205 --> 00:13:38,105
(She casually picks up her bag.)

321
00:13:38,705 --> 00:13:41,504
You know, there's a popular fashion style on the island.

322
00:13:41,505 --> 00:13:43,315
- Right. - That looks like the local style.

323
00:13:43,445 --> 00:13:45,444
- The cool-islander outfit. - That's right.

324
00:13:45,445 --> 00:13:46,884
The stylish girl on the island.

325
00:13:46,885 --> 00:13:48,485
That's the kind of outfit my mom wears.

326
00:13:48,745 --> 00:13:50,055
- Look at her. - That's right.

327
00:13:50,115 --> 00:13:52,884
Recently, there was a bazaar on the island to help...

328
00:13:52,885 --> 00:13:54,584
- abandoned dogs. - Yes.

329
00:13:54,585 --> 00:13:56,424
I was part of the bazaar too.

330
00:13:56,425 --> 00:13:57,654
- Really? - I saw your mother...

331
00:13:57,655 --> 00:13:58,655
- at the event. - Right.

332
00:13:58,656 --> 00:13:59,824
- She told me. - Really?

333
00:13:59,825 --> 00:14:01,524
She's very famous on the island.

334
00:14:01,525 --> 00:14:03,164
- Everyone knows... - The president.

335
00:14:03,165 --> 00:14:04,811
- The dog president? - that her dog is the president.

336
00:14:04,835 --> 00:14:06,294
My mom wants him to get reelected, but I don't know.

337
00:14:06,295 --> 00:14:07,664
- Wasn't it Alkong? - Already?

338
00:14:07,665 --> 00:14:08,665
No, Dalkong.

339
00:14:08,666 --> 00:14:10,004
That small dog has power.

340
00:14:10,005 --> 00:14:11,045
I'd love to see him again.

341
00:14:13,905 --> 00:14:14,975
Wait. A helmet?

342
00:14:15,605 --> 00:14:16,644
- A helmet. - What?

343
00:14:16,645 --> 00:14:18,515
(She goes somewhere while holding a helmet.)

344
00:14:21,545 --> 00:14:23,215
- It's a scooter. - I love it.

345
00:14:23,485 --> 00:14:25,085
That's all you need on Jeju Island.

346
00:14:25,215 --> 00:14:28,955
This is my favorite mode of transportation on the island.

347
00:14:29,325 --> 00:14:30,425
It's the scooter.

348
00:14:30,525 --> 00:14:34,195
I have the Class Two Small Motorcycle License.

349
00:14:34,465 --> 00:14:35,494
- On your 1st try? - I passed the test on my 1st try.

350
00:14:35,495 --> 00:14:36,995
- You got the license. - Yes.

351
00:14:38,335 --> 00:14:41,335
Didn't Sung Hwan take the test 3 or 4 times?

352
00:14:42,205 --> 00:14:43,304
- Gosh, here it is. - Wait.

353
00:14:43,305 --> 00:14:44,375
- Right. - There it is.

354
00:14:44,935 --> 00:14:47,404
You lose points if you put your feet down.

355
00:14:47,405 --> 00:14:48,445
- That was so bad. - Gosh.

356
00:14:49,575 --> 00:14:52,275
I must go out on a great day like this.

357
00:14:52,775 --> 00:14:55,414
I drive a small scooter on the island...

358
00:14:55,415 --> 00:14:58,185
as well as a big liter-class motorcycle.

359
00:14:58,515 --> 00:14:59,515
- You do? - Yes.

360
00:14:59,516 --> 00:15:00,624
We should go for a ride together.

361
00:15:00,625 --> 00:15:01,754
- Totally. - I mean it.

362
00:15:01,755 --> 00:15:03,124
- It's going to be so great. - That sounds fun.

363
00:15:03,125 --> 00:15:04,125
Let's go to Jeju Island.

364
00:15:04,225 --> 00:15:05,455
I can lift my front wheel.

365
00:15:06,125 --> 00:15:07,165
(Trembling in fear)

366
00:15:08,725 --> 00:15:11,265
(She puts on the helmet like a pro.)

367
00:15:13,405 --> 00:15:17,105
(Turning on the engine at once)

368
00:15:17,875 --> 00:15:20,305
(Vroom)

369
00:15:21,075 --> 00:15:24,115
(Let's head out.)

370
00:15:25,375 --> 00:15:28,385
(You can't be on the road without music.)

371
00:15:28,545 --> 00:15:31,085
- The weather is amazing. - Gosh, a ride by the ocean.

372
00:15:31,615 --> 00:15:33,825
- Gosh, that's so cool. - That's part of my daily life.

373
00:15:34,325 --> 00:15:35,354
- I do that every day. - There's no one around.

374
00:15:35,355 --> 00:15:36,654
That's close from my home. I do that often.

375
00:15:36,655 --> 00:15:38,031
- That's close from your home? - Yes.

376
00:15:38,055 --> 00:15:40,336
- It's close from my home. - You picked the perfect song.

377
00:15:40,695 --> 00:15:41,695
You know it, right?

378
00:15:42,525 --> 00:15:43,665
I'm already getting excited.

379
00:15:43,795 --> 00:15:44,994
You have to sing along.

380
00:15:44,995 --> 00:15:46,165
It's an immortal song.

381
00:15:47,335 --> 00:15:48,404
I love it.

382
00:15:48,405 --> 00:15:51,045
- It's a scene in a fairytale. - I feel peaceful just watching it.

383
00:15:51,575 --> 00:15:53,804
You can't feel the same vibe when you ride your bike in Seoul.

384
00:15:53,805 --> 00:15:55,504
- I mean, look at her smile. - Exactly.

385
00:15:55,505 --> 00:15:56,815
That's from genuine joy.

386
00:15:58,215 --> 00:16:01,615
Oh, my. It's summer!

387
00:16:03,815 --> 00:16:06,985
(She happily sings several songs with her nasal voice.)

388
00:16:07,655 --> 00:16:08,754
(Yu Ri arrives at a place.)

389
00:16:08,755 --> 00:16:10,555
Ddonggeul!

390
00:16:11,095 --> 00:16:12,995
Ddonggeul!

391
00:16:15,425 --> 00:16:16,894
- It's a dog. - Oh, my.

392
00:16:16,895 --> 00:16:18,534
- Gosh, so cute. - Goodness.

393
00:16:18,535 --> 00:16:20,405
- It's a brindle dog. - Ddonggeul.

394
00:16:20,805 --> 00:16:22,405
- Ddonggeul. - How cute.

395
00:16:24,305 --> 00:16:25,334
Ddonggeul.

396
00:16:25,335 --> 00:16:27,444
(Did you miss me, Ddonggeul?)

397
00:16:27,445 --> 00:16:30,221
- Can Ddonggeul stand on two feet? - Ddonggeul is so happy to see you.

398
00:16:30,245 --> 00:16:31,745
- Right. - Is it a Jindo dog?

399
00:16:32,315 --> 00:16:34,714
She's a Hogu which is a tiger-striped Jindo.

400
00:16:34,715 --> 00:16:37,614
She's a puppy at a fish farm. Her name is Ddonggeul.

401
00:16:37,615 --> 00:16:40,124
- Goodness. She likes that. - Gosh, she's showing her belly.

402
00:16:40,125 --> 00:16:41,324
- I... - She's still a baby.

403
00:16:41,325 --> 00:16:42,484
- My goodness. - She's only two.

404
00:16:42,485 --> 00:16:44,125
- That's a baby. - So she's only two.

405
00:16:44,955 --> 00:16:46,524
- Two years... - Jindo dogs show their belly...

406
00:16:46,525 --> 00:16:47,525
only to their owners.

407
00:16:47,526 --> 00:16:48,594
- Right. - Yes.

408
00:16:48,595 --> 00:16:51,664
I met her two years ago when she was a tiny puppy.

409
00:16:51,665 --> 00:16:53,064
- You met when she was a baby. - Yes.

410
00:16:53,065 --> 00:16:54,334
- I was riding my scooter. - How beautiful.

411
00:16:54,335 --> 00:16:56,081
- I spotted her and became friends. - She grew so big, so fast.

412
00:16:56,105 --> 00:16:58,374
Ddonggeul is only two years old.

413
00:16:58,375 --> 00:16:59,804
- She's so energetic... - She must be full of energy.

414
00:16:59,805 --> 00:17:01,504
- and lively. - She's full of youth.

415
00:17:01,505 --> 00:17:03,974
- The owner and workers... - Look at her.

416
00:17:03,975 --> 00:17:06,044
Work during the day.

417
00:17:06,045 --> 00:17:08,014
But I'm a freelancer.

418
00:17:08,015 --> 00:17:11,454
I sometimes go and walk her. I play with her too.

419
00:17:11,455 --> 00:17:12,684
- You play with her. - That's it.

420
00:17:12,685 --> 00:17:14,325
- How beautiful. - You're so sweet.

421
00:17:14,485 --> 00:17:17,255
I'll give you a treat. How about a treat?

422
00:17:17,795 --> 00:17:18,795
(Following her)

423
00:17:18,796 --> 00:17:20,895
- How cute. - How about a treat?

424
00:17:20,925 --> 00:17:22,495
Hello, sir.

425
00:17:23,295 --> 00:17:25,535
Sir, I'm here!

426
00:17:25,935 --> 00:17:27,765
- Sit, Ddonggeul. - Hey.

427
00:17:28,105 --> 00:17:29,864
Ddonggeul, sit. She's good at that, right?

428
00:17:29,865 --> 00:17:30,905
- Down. - Sit.

429
00:17:31,075 --> 00:17:32,075
What a cute dog.

430
00:17:33,135 --> 00:17:35,305
- Down. - Down.

431
00:17:36,845 --> 00:17:38,374
What a cutie. Well done.

432
00:17:38,375 --> 00:17:40,215
- She's so friendly. - Sir.

433
00:17:40,285 --> 00:17:41,485
I guess she knows it's me.

434
00:17:41,645 --> 00:17:43,044
- Of course. - That's why she's so happy.

435
00:17:43,045 --> 00:17:44,314
- Of course. - You come every day.

436
00:17:44,315 --> 00:17:45,391
- She waits for you. - Right?

437
00:17:45,415 --> 00:17:46,685
- It's fascinating. - My gosh.

438
00:17:46,925 --> 00:17:47,954
- She can tell... - She knows everything.

439
00:17:47,955 --> 00:17:48,984
I'm coming by the engine sound.

440
00:17:48,985 --> 00:17:50,024
- She knows it's me. - Yes.

441
00:17:50,025 --> 00:17:51,055
- That's right. - Yes.

442
00:17:51,195 --> 00:17:52,915
She can tell it's you even from a distance.

443
00:17:52,955 --> 00:17:55,295
Ddonggeul. You're so cute.

444
00:17:55,725 --> 00:17:56,885
Get some water. And we'll go.

445
00:17:59,765 --> 00:18:02,465
Let's go for a walk.

446
00:18:03,975 --> 00:18:05,174
- Let's go. - I see. You...

447
00:18:05,175 --> 00:18:06,804
- Yes. I walk her. - You walk her?

448
00:18:06,805 --> 00:18:09,505
- Gosh, the owner must be so happy. - Let's go for a walk.

449
00:18:09,605 --> 00:18:13,215
That's why he sometimes gives me octopus.

450
00:18:13,945 --> 00:18:16,815
- He wants to thank me. - Do you walk her often?

451
00:18:17,115 --> 00:18:19,384
Yes, I walk her when I'm there. At least once a day.

452
00:18:19,385 --> 00:18:20,555
At least once a day?

453
00:18:21,025 --> 00:18:22,684
Are you working as a dogwalker as a side hustle?

454
00:18:22,685 --> 00:18:23,794
No.

455
00:18:23,795 --> 00:18:25,355
I think it might be your part-time job.

456
00:18:25,425 --> 00:18:26,824
- I just like doing that. - You just like that?

457
00:18:26,825 --> 00:18:29,294
- I like the neighborhood dogs. - Right. That's...

458
00:18:29,295 --> 00:18:30,565
And they like me too.

459
00:18:31,695 --> 00:18:32,765
Let's go.

460
00:18:33,495 --> 00:18:34,905
Let's go!

461
00:18:35,165 --> 00:18:36,804
Ddonggeul is super friendly.

462
00:18:36,805 --> 00:18:38,375
- She's a sweet one. - Ddonggeul.

463
00:18:42,205 --> 00:18:43,645
Great job.

464
00:18:44,245 --> 00:18:46,145
Ddonggeul, you're a pro at this.

465
00:18:47,885 --> 00:18:48,885
Ddonggeul.

466
00:18:52,615 --> 00:18:54,555
Ddonggeul. How is it possible...

467
00:18:54,655 --> 00:18:58,425
that you can walk so calmly like this?

468
00:18:59,595 --> 00:19:01,264
I can tell she does this often.

469
00:19:01,265 --> 00:19:02,994
- They both know each other's pace. - Right.

470
00:19:02,995 --> 00:19:04,835
- They know each other's gait. - Yes, they do.

471
00:19:05,135 --> 00:19:07,165
(Grinning)

472
00:19:10,975 --> 00:19:12,405
(Patting)

473
00:19:12,675 --> 00:19:14,245
It's hot, right? Let's hurry.

474
00:19:14,375 --> 00:19:15,745
Let's walk fast. Go.

475
00:19:16,305 --> 00:19:19,045
One, two.

476
00:19:20,645 --> 00:19:22,314
- That's a real run. - Ddonggeul must be so happy.

477
00:19:22,315 --> 00:19:23,814
Exactly. She must be a happy dog.

478
00:19:23,815 --> 00:19:25,575
- Ddonggeul is matching my pace. - Let's go.

479
00:19:25,655 --> 00:19:27,185
Ddonggeul, thank you...

480
00:19:27,655 --> 00:19:29,085
for matching my pace.

481
00:19:30,695 --> 00:19:32,295
We're back. Yes?

482
00:19:32,795 --> 00:19:34,595
- Did she have fun? - Yes, totally.

483
00:19:36,595 --> 00:19:37,795
She can't stop looking at you.

484
00:19:40,135 --> 00:19:42,435
- Sir, I'll be back tomorrow. - Yes? Sure.

485
00:19:43,065 --> 00:19:44,074
Walk her again tomorrow.

486
00:19:44,075 --> 00:19:45,634
(Wagging her tail)

487
00:19:45,635 --> 00:19:47,405
Look at her wagging her tail. Oh, my.

488
00:19:47,505 --> 00:19:49,875
I bet Ddonggeul always waits for this time of the day.

489
00:19:50,515 --> 00:19:52,675
Bye. See you. The walk is over.

490
00:19:53,445 --> 00:19:55,044
I'm off. See you around.

491
00:19:55,045 --> 00:19:56,245
- Bye. - Bye.

492
00:19:57,715 --> 00:20:00,525
(She goes to the next spot after saying goodbye to Ddonggeul.)

493
00:20:01,485 --> 00:20:03,224
- I'm off, sir. - See you.

494
00:20:03,225 --> 00:20:04,325
Bye.

495
00:20:10,395 --> 00:20:12,465
Oh, the smell of the sea urchins.

496
00:20:13,535 --> 00:20:15,165
I can smell the sea urchins.

497
00:20:15,265 --> 00:20:17,334
- Sea urchins. - It's the sea urchin season.

498
00:20:17,335 --> 00:20:18,775
I'd love to have sea urchin noodles.

499
00:20:19,905 --> 00:20:22,675
(While breathing in the smell of the Jeju ocean, )

500
00:20:23,845 --> 00:20:26,275
(she eagerly rides her scooter and arrives at some place.)

501
00:20:27,245 --> 00:20:30,045
(I'm here!)

502
00:20:31,815 --> 00:20:35,925
(Striding in)

503
00:20:37,225 --> 00:20:39,824
- Hello. - Welcome.

504
00:20:39,825 --> 00:20:42,164
- You're here. - I'm here.

505
00:20:42,165 --> 00:20:43,595
- Hello. - You're here.

506
00:20:43,765 --> 00:20:45,894
- Ma'am. - She went to the restroom.

507
00:20:45,895 --> 00:20:48,205
This is my go-to restaurant on the island.

508
00:20:48,905 --> 00:20:51,675
I became close to the owners of the restaurant after moving here.

509
00:20:51,975 --> 00:20:54,604
And just like me, they have an acting career.

510
00:20:54,605 --> 00:20:56,805
We have a lot of similar interests.

511
00:20:57,015 --> 00:20:59,444
When I first decided to settle down here,

512
00:20:59,445 --> 00:21:02,415
they helped me a lot, so my relocation process...

513
00:21:02,515 --> 00:21:05,915
would go smoothly. They helped me become independent.

514
00:21:06,515 --> 00:21:07,755
I'm here.

515
00:21:08,355 --> 00:21:09,654
Gosh, the kids are here.

516
00:21:09,655 --> 00:21:11,194
- Hey. - Hello.

517
00:21:11,195 --> 00:21:13,024
- Hello, Seung Woo. - Hello.

518
00:21:13,025 --> 00:21:14,395
- Hello. - Hi.

519
00:21:14,495 --> 00:21:16,024
- You're friends with everyone. - Hi.

520
00:21:16,025 --> 00:21:17,635
We're all neighbors.

521
00:21:17,765 --> 00:21:19,194
- Chief Kwon. - The neighborhood.

522
00:21:19,195 --> 00:21:20,864
- Right. That's my nickname. - It's like "Hometown Cha-Cha-Cha."

523
00:21:20,865 --> 00:21:23,146
- She's the neighborhood chief. - "Hometown Cha-Cha-Cha."

524
00:21:24,035 --> 00:21:25,435
- I... - What do you want to eat?

525
00:21:26,635 --> 00:21:28,474
- I'm so hungry. - What did you do today?

526
00:21:28,475 --> 00:21:29,845
I'm so hungry.

527
00:21:30,075 --> 00:21:31,845
(What should I eat?)

528
00:21:32,545 --> 00:21:34,815
Did you guys eat? Did your husband and mom eat?

529
00:21:35,545 --> 00:21:37,655
- We haven't eaten yet. - Let's eat together then.

530
00:21:37,985 --> 00:21:39,715
Okay. I want the octopus ramyeon.

531
00:21:39,815 --> 00:21:40,924
- Ramyeon? - I haven't had it in a while.

532
00:21:40,925 --> 00:21:42,085
I must have some ramyeon.

533
00:21:42,685 --> 00:21:44,224
Okay.

534
00:21:44,225 --> 00:21:45,745
(She places her order like a regular.)

535
00:21:48,995 --> 00:21:50,094
(She grabs the side dishes like it's nothing new.)

536
00:21:50,095 --> 00:21:51,464
- You guys are real friends. - Yes, we're close.

537
00:21:51,465 --> 00:21:53,264
- Right. - She serves her own food.

538
00:21:53,265 --> 00:21:54,265
- Yes. - This is nice.

539
00:21:54,265 --> 00:21:55,265
(Comfortable)

540
00:21:55,266 --> 00:21:56,305
This is nice.

541
00:21:56,965 --> 00:21:58,875
I'm hungry. Let's eat together.

542
00:21:59,075 --> 00:22:00,304
There will be too much food for me.

543
00:22:00,305 --> 00:22:02,374
(Octopus ramyeon arrives!)

544
00:22:02,375 --> 00:22:03,375
Here it is.

545
00:22:03,375 --> 00:22:04,375
(Excited)

546
00:22:04,376 --> 00:22:05,645
Here it is.

547
00:22:07,085 --> 00:22:08,544
(It's full of seafood from the Jeju Island's sea.)

548
00:22:08,545 --> 00:22:09,585
It looks so delicious.

549
00:22:10,455 --> 00:22:11,584
- This is insane. - Seriously.

550
00:22:11,585 --> 00:22:12,615
It's a whole octopus.

551
00:22:12,985 --> 00:22:14,065
- Clams. - Octopus ramyeon.

552
00:22:14,555 --> 00:22:15,624
(It makes her mouth water.)

553
00:22:15,625 --> 00:22:17,401
I haven't had ramyeon with white soup in a while.

554
00:22:17,425 --> 00:22:18,954
I'm so hungry.

555
00:22:18,955 --> 00:22:21,094
- It looks so tasty. - Enjoy it.

556
00:22:21,095 --> 00:22:22,494
(A heap of food)

557
00:22:22,495 --> 00:22:23,595
Go ahead and eat.

558
00:22:24,495 --> 00:22:27,465
Thank you for the food. You gave me a big abalone.

559
00:22:27,765 --> 00:22:29,134
- Go ahead and eat. - It looks delicious.

560
00:22:29,135 --> 00:22:30,674
- This is insane. - Thank you for the food.

561
00:22:30,675 --> 00:22:31,675
(Gulping)

562
00:22:34,505 --> 00:22:36,374
(Trying a spoonful of soup)

563
00:22:36,375 --> 00:22:37,375
(Impressed)

564
00:22:39,075 --> 00:22:40,115
This is the taste I like.

565
00:22:42,715 --> 00:22:44,015
They're eating together.

566
00:22:44,085 --> 00:22:46,015
- Yes. - They're like a family.

567
00:22:47,055 --> 00:22:49,884
Thankfully, it was between lunch and dinner.

568
00:22:49,885 --> 00:22:50,894
- Ramyeon is best for that time. - It was...

569
00:22:50,895 --> 00:22:53,625
time for them to eat.

570
00:22:56,225 --> 00:22:58,665
(She begins inhaling the noodles in earnest.)

571
00:22:59,835 --> 00:23:05,075
(Slurping)

572
00:23:06,635 --> 00:23:07,845
She eats with gusto.

573
00:23:08,105 --> 00:23:09,774
Yu Ri eats a big amount of food.

574
00:23:09,775 --> 00:23:11,375
- That's right. - Yes. She is like that.

575
00:23:13,275 --> 00:23:16,285
(Let's see.)

576
00:23:18,055 --> 00:23:19,185
Don't we need more?

577
00:23:20,055 --> 00:23:21,324
- We need more, right? - I think we do.

578
00:23:21,325 --> 00:23:22,684
- Honestly, this isn't enough. - Honestly, this isn't enough.

579
00:23:22,685 --> 00:23:23,785
I agree.

580
00:23:24,325 --> 00:23:25,554
- Go ahead. - Should we mix it with rice...

581
00:23:25,555 --> 00:23:26,624
- in here? - No.

582
00:23:26,625 --> 00:23:27,664
(The second dish, stir-fried octopus gets served.)

583
00:23:27,665 --> 00:23:28,795
Look at the seasoning.

584
00:23:29,125 --> 00:23:30,164
- They're good. - That's the real deal.

585
00:23:30,165 --> 00:23:32,435
- They're good. - The seasoning is dark in color.

586
00:23:33,565 --> 00:23:34,705
- Really? - I'll do it.

587
00:23:35,205 --> 00:23:36,485
- I'll do it well. - Here we go.

588
00:23:39,235 --> 00:23:42,045
This stir-fried dish has a smoky flavor.

589
00:23:42,805 --> 00:23:44,274
It has a smoky flavor.

590
00:23:44,275 --> 00:23:46,355
- It looks like it does. - This is driving me crazy.

591
00:23:48,045 --> 00:23:50,015
- It smells good. - High heat makes it tasty.

592
00:23:50,315 --> 00:23:51,385
Exactly.

593
00:23:51,585 --> 00:23:54,654
Mom said she'd give me her recipe.

594
00:23:54,655 --> 00:23:55,824
Knowing her for three years won't be enough.

595
00:23:55,825 --> 00:23:57,294
It won't be enough.

596
00:23:57,295 --> 00:23:59,025
You'll need to work as a server.

597
00:23:59,195 --> 00:24:00,595
- Work as a server? - That's right.

598
00:24:01,025 --> 00:24:02,594
I want to know her recipe for the broth...

599
00:24:02,595 --> 00:24:03,864
- and sauce. - It has a smoky flavor.

600
00:24:03,865 --> 00:24:05,145
- But she won't teach you. - No.

601
00:24:05,495 --> 00:24:07,864
Even if you cook with the same ingredients in Seoul,

602
00:24:07,865 --> 00:24:09,534
- it won't taste the same. - The ingredients will be different.

603
00:24:09,535 --> 00:24:11,375
The ingredients are so fresh there.

604
00:24:11,875 --> 00:24:13,304
I think I have a clue.

605
00:24:13,305 --> 00:24:15,604
(Let's forget about the recipe and mix the dish with rice.)

606
00:24:15,605 --> 00:24:16,705
I don't want to watch this.

607
00:24:17,215 --> 00:24:18,521
- For what? - For a smoky flavor.

608
00:24:18,545 --> 00:24:20,615
(Opening her mouth wide)

609
00:24:21,715 --> 00:24:23,485
(The taste makes her clap.)

610
00:24:23,845 --> 00:24:25,554
The combination of these two dishes is insane.

611
00:24:25,555 --> 00:24:26,685
- I know. - Right?

612
00:24:27,585 --> 00:24:28,985
I see why you live on Jeju Island.

613
00:24:29,255 --> 00:24:30,895
You want to eat tasty food.

614
00:24:32,525 --> 00:24:34,325
You should set up some laver flakes, right?

615
00:24:34,595 --> 00:24:36,624
- You said what I wanted to say. - Seriously.

616
00:24:36,625 --> 00:24:39,094
- We're practically eating together. - That's right.

617
00:24:39,095 --> 00:24:40,134
Yes.

618
00:24:40,135 --> 00:24:41,734
I'm setting up some laver flakes.

619
00:24:41,735 --> 00:24:42,815
I'm sprinkling some pepper.

620
00:24:43,435 --> 00:24:44,634
They're like two large babies.

621
00:24:44,635 --> 00:24:46,804
(They're like two large babies.)

622
00:24:46,805 --> 00:24:49,004
I'm eating it with dried laver in my imagination.

623
00:24:49,005 --> 00:24:50,715
I'm getting a spoonful.

624
00:24:53,075 --> 00:24:54,544
(It's as tasty as I expected.)

625
00:24:54,545 --> 00:24:55,545
It's as I expected.

626
00:24:57,385 --> 00:24:58,654
You need to eat some rice.

627
00:24:58,655 --> 00:25:00,455
(Scraping the bottom of the bowl)

628
00:25:04,455 --> 00:25:05,525
It was a nice meal.

629
00:25:09,065 --> 00:25:14,065
(As if she is used to it, she cleans up after herself.)

630
00:25:16,165 --> 00:25:17,904
(Lifting)

631
00:25:17,905 --> 00:25:20,575
- They're like a family. - I know. They're her family.

632
00:25:22,375 --> 00:25:23,975
It'll feel incredible to nap there.

633
00:25:24,145 --> 00:25:25,415
- I've napped there. - Nice.

634
00:25:25,845 --> 00:25:27,074
- You should lie down right away. - When there are no customers...

635
00:25:27,075 --> 00:25:29,195
- on a rainy day... - She is like a part-timer there.

636
00:25:30,755 --> 00:25:33,615
This kimchi tastes incredible with ramyeon.

637
00:25:34,885 --> 00:25:36,084
(Slapping)

638
00:25:36,085 --> 00:25:38,255
I'm so happy to hear that.

639
00:25:39,295 --> 00:25:41,125
- It smells incredible, right? - It's nice.

640
00:25:41,825 --> 00:25:44,694
Eat young radish kimchi with spicy noodles.

641
00:25:44,695 --> 00:25:47,605
- It'll be good with noodles. - Young radish kimchi naengmyeon.

642
00:25:47,865 --> 00:25:49,835
- There is a thin film of ice. - Yes.

643
00:25:51,575 --> 00:25:53,775
Being on Jeju Island isn't the only good thing.

644
00:25:54,205 --> 00:25:56,885
- Being surrounded by people... - Those people are so nice. I know.

645
00:25:57,745 --> 00:25:59,744
Here they are

646
00:25:59,745 --> 00:26:01,815
I'll enjoy them

647
00:26:04,085 --> 00:26:05,485
I'll think of you every time I eat.

648
00:26:05,615 --> 00:26:06,654
Here.

649
00:26:06,655 --> 00:26:08,354
(She pays for her meal.)

650
00:26:08,355 --> 00:26:09,385
She pays right away.

651
00:26:13,025 --> 00:26:14,395
Soo Hyun, why...

652
00:26:14,925 --> 00:26:16,525
What? Didn't it go through?

653
00:26:17,195 --> 00:26:18,434
- It's just for octopus ramyeon. - Did she charge 1,000 dollars?

654
00:26:18,435 --> 00:26:20,635
- Did you get ripped off? - Don't be ridiculous.

655
00:26:21,265 --> 00:26:22,345
I bet she paid 460 dollars.

656
00:26:22,565 --> 00:26:24,135
We're close. For goodness' sake.

657
00:26:24,905 --> 00:26:26,874
It's just for octopus ramyeon. I ate stir-fried octopus too.

658
00:26:26,875 --> 00:26:28,004
(I ate stir-fried octopus too. Why is the bill so small?)

659
00:26:28,005 --> 00:26:29,205
- It's fine. - Seriously.

660
00:26:31,375 --> 00:26:32,515
Seriously.

661
00:26:33,475 --> 00:26:35,084
- Gosh, she is cool. - She is cool.

662
00:26:35,085 --> 00:26:37,165
Soo Hyun is totally cool. She has a girl-crush vibe.

663
00:26:38,585 --> 00:26:39,984
You're so funny.

664
00:26:39,985 --> 00:26:42,065
- See you tomorrow. - That kind of love is rare now.

665
00:26:44,895 --> 00:26:47,365
Hyun Bin, I'm leaving. Mom, thank you for the food.

666
00:26:47,425 --> 00:26:48,524
- Okay. Bye. - Bye.

667
00:26:48,525 --> 00:26:50,065
- Bye. - Take care.

668
00:26:50,365 --> 00:26:52,135
- I'm leaving. Don't come outside. - Okay.

669
00:26:53,365 --> 00:26:55,205
- Drive safely. - Okay, I will.

670
00:26:55,865 --> 00:26:56,904
At all times.

671
00:26:56,905 --> 00:26:58,405
At all times,

672
00:26:58,535 --> 00:27:00,175
I'll drive safely.

673
00:27:00,945 --> 00:27:02,545
- Watch out for the cars. - Okay.

674
00:27:02,845 --> 00:27:05,645
- She is like an older sister. - I know. She is my older sister.

675
00:27:07,845 --> 00:27:11,555
(I'm leaving.)

676
00:27:13,255 --> 00:27:15,855
(Driving)

677
00:27:17,025 --> 00:27:18,495
What time is it now? It's 5pm.

678
00:27:18,725 --> 00:27:21,464
The tide is low at 6pm.

679
00:27:21,465 --> 00:27:22,724
It'll be at its lowest.

680
00:27:22,725 --> 00:27:24,711
- Where is she going? - I'll be able to find it, right?

681
00:27:24,735 --> 00:27:25,934
- Will you harvest something? - Yes.

682
00:27:25,935 --> 00:27:28,265
- I check the tide often. - Is she really a haenyeo?

683
00:27:28,465 --> 00:27:30,104
- What? - There must be something.

684
00:27:30,105 --> 00:27:31,135
Seriously. No way.

685
00:27:33,805 --> 00:27:35,004
- Will she go into the water? - I think she will.

686
00:27:35,005 --> 00:27:36,944
- There are skin divers... - She'll go into the water.

687
00:27:36,945 --> 00:27:37,975
Behind her.

688
00:27:41,885 --> 00:27:42,915
I'm here!

689
00:27:45,315 --> 00:27:46,315
Let's see.

690
00:27:46,316 --> 00:27:48,955
(Taking out)

691
00:27:50,125 --> 00:27:51,155
Let's see.

692
00:27:55,165 --> 00:28:00,665
(She arrives at the beach with a mesh bag.)

693
00:28:02,305 --> 00:28:04,035
(Oh, my!)

694
00:28:06,035 --> 00:28:07,334
(The blue Jeju Island's sea)

695
00:28:07,335 --> 00:28:08,505
That's my mart.

696
00:28:09,245 --> 00:28:11,374
- Your mart. - It's so nice. It's your mart.

697
00:28:11,375 --> 00:28:12,444
Yes.

698
00:28:12,445 --> 00:28:14,315
(Rolling up)

699
00:28:16,345 --> 00:28:18,755
(She ties her hair haphazardly.)

700
00:28:21,325 --> 00:28:23,785
(She puts on gloves.)

701
00:28:31,335 --> 00:28:32,395
Here is hijiki.

702
00:28:32,635 --> 00:28:34,071
- Hijiki? Will you harvest hijiki? - I think...

703
00:28:34,095 --> 00:28:35,135
- Hijiki. - Hijiki?

704
00:28:35,305 --> 00:28:37,035
These days...

705
00:28:37,335 --> 00:28:41,544
I went to the Sumapo Coast to harvest some plump hijiki.

706
00:28:41,545 --> 00:28:44,145
I heard that there was a lot of hijiki,

707
00:28:44,775 --> 00:28:47,415
so I went there to harvest it.

708
00:28:48,315 --> 00:28:49,485
It's hijiki.

709
00:28:49,945 --> 00:28:52,455
- It had hijiki on its head. - I see.

710
00:28:52,655 --> 00:28:56,384
There are a lot of sea snails and hijiki these days.

711
00:28:56,385 --> 00:28:58,354
You can also find blue crabs.

712
00:28:58,355 --> 00:28:59,854
- Blue crabs? - Yes. Blue crabs are in season...

713
00:28:59,855 --> 00:29:01,265
- these days. - Blue crabs.

714
00:29:01,465 --> 00:29:03,095
They're blue-colored crabs.

715
00:29:03,265 --> 00:29:04,894
It really is a mart. It has all the seasonal ingredients.

716
00:29:04,895 --> 00:29:06,134
- It's a mart. - It really is...

717
00:29:06,135 --> 00:29:08,364
a mart that gives freely.

718
00:29:08,365 --> 00:29:10,135
- I see. - You get food from nature.

719
00:29:11,535 --> 00:29:13,174
- Can you take it as you want? - No.

720
00:29:13,175 --> 00:29:15,644
You can only harvest it in designated areas.

721
00:29:15,645 --> 00:29:17,144
- I see. - The permitted areas.

722
00:29:17,145 --> 00:29:18,851
You can only harvest it in permitted areas.

723
00:29:18,875 --> 00:29:20,114
So you can't take it as you want.

724
00:29:20,115 --> 00:29:21,675
- No, you can't. - You'll get arrested.

725
00:29:22,445 --> 00:29:23,515
This is incredible.

726
00:29:23,885 --> 00:29:26,155
- Anyone can do it. - You can harvest it like that.

727
00:29:27,885 --> 00:29:29,055
It's hijiki.

728
00:29:30,755 --> 00:29:32,694
(There is hijiki everywhere.)

729
00:29:32,695 --> 00:29:34,625
There is so much.

730
00:29:36,295 --> 00:29:38,695
(She turns greedy.)

731
00:29:40,465 --> 00:29:42,105
It's like a gold mine!

732
00:29:42,165 --> 00:29:43,905
(They don't pay her any mind.)

733
00:29:44,505 --> 00:29:46,274
(This mart has good hijiki.)

734
00:29:46,275 --> 00:29:48,205
Isn't Yu Ri a natural person?

735
00:29:49,245 --> 00:29:50,774
- She is so easygoing. - Still,

736
00:29:50,775 --> 00:29:52,745
it suits her. She has a cool life.

737
00:29:54,075 --> 00:29:55,245
This is enough.

738
00:29:55,785 --> 00:29:56,985
This is more than enough.

739
00:29:57,685 --> 00:29:59,515
If I want more, I can always come back.

740
00:30:01,125 --> 00:30:02,125
I got too much.

741
00:30:02,126 --> 00:30:03,384
- She got a lot. - It's a lot.

742
00:30:03,385 --> 00:30:04,395
Let's go.

743
00:30:04,855 --> 00:30:05,955
I need to go now.

744
00:30:06,125 --> 00:30:07,765
Is it 6:30pm? I need to hurry up.

745
00:30:10,425 --> 00:30:12,795
(Hurrying)

746
00:30:13,465 --> 00:30:14,935
Where is Chief Kwon going now?

747
00:30:15,765 --> 00:30:17,204
- Chief Kwon is busy. - Chief Kwon.

748
00:30:17,205 --> 00:30:18,374
- She is so busy. - On Jeju Island,

749
00:30:18,375 --> 00:30:19,735
- I'm so busy. - Good.

750
00:30:20,875 --> 00:30:23,105
(She hangs the harvested hijiki at the front.)

751
00:30:24,415 --> 00:30:28,515
(Chief Kwon sets off again.)

752
00:30:30,745 --> 00:30:32,355
- The sun is setting. - How cool.

753
00:30:32,485 --> 00:30:34,584
The sun sets so quickly.

754
00:30:34,585 --> 00:30:35,905
- It really does. - You're right.

755
00:30:37,455 --> 00:30:38,695
All right.

756
00:30:38,995 --> 00:30:40,524
She came home after visiting a mart.

757
00:30:40,525 --> 00:30:42,765
(Chief Kwon returns home after grocery shopping.)

758
00:30:46,435 --> 00:30:49,165
(Taking out)

759
00:30:49,365 --> 00:30:50,434
Here.

760
00:30:50,435 --> 00:30:51,435
That's good.

761
00:30:51,436 --> 00:30:53,356
(She puts the mesh bag with hijiki in the sink.)

762
00:30:54,275 --> 00:30:58,715
(I don't have much time.)

763
00:31:00,545 --> 00:31:01,645
What time is it now?

764
00:31:01,915 --> 00:31:03,035
What does she want to watch?

765
00:31:04,615 --> 00:31:05,684
- What? - Baseball?

766
00:31:05,685 --> 00:31:07,255
(Baseball?)

767
00:31:07,485 --> 00:31:09,084
- Which team are you a fan of? - You're a baseball fan.

768
00:31:09,085 --> 00:31:10,284
(It's nice to meet you.)

769
00:31:10,285 --> 00:31:11,454
I'm a fan of Hanwha Eagles.

770
00:31:11,455 --> 00:31:13,424
- Eagles? - Hanwha Eagles?

771
00:31:13,425 --> 00:31:14,495
That's right.

772
00:31:14,965 --> 00:31:16,485
My team will catch up with yours soon.

773
00:31:17,065 --> 00:31:19,634
- They have a long way to go. - It'll happen soon.

774
00:31:19,635 --> 00:31:21,315
- Right now... - They need to be diligent.

775
00:31:21,435 --> 00:31:22,834
- Your team is ranked higher. - Of course.

776
00:31:22,835 --> 00:31:24,135
- They placed second. - Yes.

